Subject: [PATCH 6/6] [compiler-rt] Include the POSIX locking headers on a Windows target

lib/profile picks its file-locking implementation from a configure check that
compiles a small program against <fcntl.h>. On a Windows target whose libc is
sprt that check succeeds - sprt implements POSIX advisory record locking on top
of LockFileEx - so COMPILER_RT_HAS_FCNTL_LCK is defined and lprofLockFd takes
the fcntl path.

That path does not build there. InstrProfilingUtil.c reaches for <fcntl.h> only
in its non-Windows include branch, so fcntl, F_WRLCK and F_SETLKW are undeclared,
and WindowsMMap.h has already renamed flock to its own LockFileEx shim with

  #define flock __llvm_profile_flock

which turns the `struct flock` the fcntl path declares into an incomplete type.
Upstream never sees this because on MSVC the configure check fails and the shim
is what gets used.

Pull the three headers in when the check has selected that path, and drop the
flock macro with it. The shim is only reached from the branch fcntl supersedes -
the two are the arms of one #ifdef/#elif - so nothing else in the file loses it.

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c b/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c
index 0fae91cfb..274ac68b5 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/profile/InstrProfilingUtil.c
@@ -11,6 +11,18 @@
 #include <process.h>
 #include <windows.h>
 #include "WindowsMMap.h"
+#ifdef COMPILER_RT_HAS_FCNTL_LCK
+/* A Windows target whose libc still offers POSIX advisory record locking, so
+   the configure check selected the fcntl path below. Its declarations are in
+   headers this branch does not otherwise pull in, and WindowsMMap.h renames
+   flock to its own LockFileEx shim, which would turn struct flock into an
+   incomplete type. The shim is only called from the branch that fcntl
+   supersedes, so dropping the macro here costs nothing. */
+#undef flock
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
 #else
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
